# Trust Model

This document explains the trust model of xLaDe

---

## Categories

1. Cryptographic Keys
2. Official Website
3. Distribution
4. Components
5. Dependencies

---

## Keys

- It includes our PGP key and SSH key
- The canonical source to get keys is official website
- Compare the keys of repository and other sources to official website key
- If onion site, project and other source keys match, then only keys are trusted
- If any single key is different, then inform to us
- The PGP key can be verified from founder's website also
- In case the keys are compromised, we will mention on our site and will publish new keys

---

## The Onion Service

- The onion service address is derived from a cryptographic key
- Official website is trusted
- This asssumption works till the private key is safe
- In case onion site is not under our control, we will inform in other available project signed with PGP key
- Only trust such a message if that message file is signed by us

---

## Distribution

- No centralised sources are trusted
- We publish checksum of both zip files and tar balls in our website
- Compare them against the files you get
- Sources not mentioned in docs/official_sources are untrusted
- In case the checksums are different, report to us
- We will investigate and put the correct file or checksum in case of problem

---

## Components

- The CLI is trusted 
- The scripts and files are assumed to work as intended
- We assume the workflows and tests are working
- In case of divergence from intended function, they will be updated
- A security advisory will be issued if required 

---

## Dependencies

- Lean 4 is trusted
- The external dependencies such as Python, black, flake8, etc. are assumed to be working as intended 
- Untrusted dependencies are outside our project scope

---

## Misc

- In case of an attacker having control of multiple sources of xLaDe and no way of authorisation, founder's official website will be authoritative
- This is in-case of extreme failure when keys and official website of xLaDe both are down
- The trust in site comes from the fact that founder's site is onion site, which is derived from cryptographic identity, so it verifies itself
- However, such a situation should not arise under normal conditions

---
